  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply recorded $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 47,559 awards with an average award size of $60.6K. Obligations fell 51.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $2.8B. Other buying agencies include the General Services Administration at $78.7M, the Department of State at $21.2M, and the Department of Homeland Security at $21.1M. Market activity is concentrated in a few NAICS categories. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounted for $1.7B, and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing accounted for $838M. Year-by-year obligations show prior peaks and troughs: FY21 was $2.9B, FY22 was $3.1B, FY23 was $4.6B, FY24 was $4.8B, and FY25 was $6B. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. The figures here are contract obligations except where a specific table lists total contract values, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Atlantic Diving Supply's federal business changed over time?",
        "body": "Atlantic Diving Supply's obligations were $2.9B in FY21, $3.1B in FY22, $4.6B in FY23, $4.8B in FY24, $6B in FY25, and $2.9B in FY26 to date. Obligations fell 51.9% year over year in the current fiscal year to date. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $60.6K across 47,559 awards. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and what markets drive Atlantic Diving Supply's sales?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Other top buyers include the General Services Administration at $78.7M, the Department of State at $21.2M, and the Department of Homeland Security at $21.1M. The largest markets by NAICS are Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $1.7B and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $838M. Several smaller manufacturing categories also appear, including Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $95.3M and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $37.2M."
      }
    ]
